"\"use strict\";Object.defineProperty(exports,\"__esModule\",{value:true});Object.defineProperty(exports,\"default\",{enumerable:true,get:function(){return MDXContent}});function _extends(){_extends=Object.assign||function(target){for(var i=1;i<arguments.length;i++){var source=arguments[i];for(var key in source){if(Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(source,key)){target[key]=source[key]}}}return target};return _extends.apply(this,arguments)}function _createMdxContent(props){var _components=_extends({a:\"a\",blockquote:\"blockquote\",em:\"em\",h2:\"h2\",p:\"p\",strong:\"strong\"},props.components);return Vue.h(Vue.Fragment,null,Vue.h(_components.h2,null,\"Introduction\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"Epheia (依菲雅，/ɪˈfiːə/) used she or they pronouns. She was transgender, and queer too.\",Vue.h(\"sup\",null,Vue.h(\"a\",{href:\"#footnote-1\",id:\"footnote-ref-1\"},\"1\"))),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"She loved yuri (girls’ love) in anime and related media, as well as simulation games and rail transit, especially route planning.\",Vue.h(\"sup\",null,Vue.h(\"a\",{href:\"#footnote-2\",id:\"footnote-ref-2\"},\"2\")),\" After being assigned to a new class in high school, she had five dorm roommates who were all very “cishet” (cisgender and straight). Just hearing the topics they talked about irritated her.\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.blockquote,null,\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"I started watching yuri anime with my headphones on and didn’t initiate conversations with them.\"),\"\\n\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"She could build her own websites and write code, and she kept her articles, diaries, and archived tweets on her own sites.\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"She also founded TransCircle (跨环), a project documenting the stories of the Chinese-speaking MtF transgender community.\",Vue.h(\"sup\",null,Vue.h(\"a\",{href:\"#footnote-3\",id:\"footnote-ref-3\"},\"3\"))),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.h2,null,\"Where Her Name Came From\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"She really liked Castorice, a character in \",Vue.h(_components.em,null,\"Honkai: Star Rail\"),\". Unlike many other Castorice fans, her reason for liking her was this:\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.blockquote,null,\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"I really wish I could become someone like Castorice.\"),\"\\n\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"She had always been drawn to a “sense of the sacred,” and Castorice was exactly that kind of character. The yuri story between Castorice and her younger sister, Polyxia, also moved her deeply.\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"In the game, Castorice has the codename EpieiKeia216. She adapted it into Epheia. She came up with the name together with AI, making several “gacha pulls”—trying again for a new result—before she was satisfied.\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.blockquote,null,\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"Mm, Epheia it is.\"),\"\\n\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"Only later did she learn that the word was pronounced differently from what she had imagined. Still, she kept her own pronunciation and included a pronunciation guide wherever she used the name. She then chose a Chinese name, “依菲雅” (Yīfēiyǎ), to match the sound, and gave that name to the catgirl character she had designed as well.\",Vue.h(\"sup\",null,Vue.h(\"a\",{href:\"#footnote-4\",id:\"footnote-ref-4\"},\"4\"))),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.h2,null,\"Becoming Herself\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"Even in kindergarten, she had imagined being a girl and wanted to wear cute dresses. After starting primary school, she tried hard to fit in with the boys, but inwardly she had always envied the girls.\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"One rainy day in middle school, she was walking back to the classroom from the restroom, trailing her hand along a railing and sweeping the droplets on it into a stream. The student on duty accused her of “leaning over the railing” and wanted to dock points. She went to the moral education office to appeal. The director checked the surveillance footage and finally said:\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.blockquote,null,\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"“All right, I’ll cancel that point deduction. But from now on, I’ll be keeping a special eye on you. If you break any school rules, I’ll dock double the points.”\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"I was terrified. Anxious, and in despair.\"),\"\\n\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"That afternoon, the director called her in for another talk. She explained her worries, but the director just smiled: “Oh, you actually believed that?” The hopes she had once held for school were completely shattered, just like that.\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"This incident, together with some things that happened afterward, made her begin to question everything she had once believed. She set herself a principle: “Freedom is the right to do anything that does not harm others.”\",Vue.h(\"sup\",null,Vue.h(\"a\",{href:\"#footnote-5\",id:\"footnote-ref-5\"},\"5\")),\" Later, while scrolling, she came across some MtF posts and felt as though she had “found something.” She gave herself “three years to explore.”\",Vue.h(\"sup\",null,Vue.h(\"a\",{href:\"#footnote-6\",id:\"footnote-ref-6\"},\"6\"))),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"Around March 2026, she finally began talking to her mom about this. Her mom said she would support her no matter what she chose, and that gave her a great deal of courage. She updated her Twitter bio:\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.blockquote,null,\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"Huge fan of 2D yuri | \\uD83C\\uDFF3️‍\\uD83C\\uDF08\\uD83C\\uDFF3️‍⚧️LGBT-friendly | ’09 | MtF? MtX? Still exploring; at any rate, not a cishet guy | Not on HRT yet | Parentally supported | Vibe coding | Building websites\"),\"\\n\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"Within just a few hours, several MtF people had followed her. On March 20, she went to a hospital outpatient clinic for the first time.\",Vue.h(\"sup\",null,Vue.h(\"a\",{href:\"#footnote-3\",id:\"footnote-ref-3\"},\"3\"))),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"On March 30, before starting HRT, she wrote about other trans sisters in her diary:\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.blockquote,null,\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"They go through so much, just to be themselves.\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"They’re so brave.\"),\"\\n\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"At the time, she still felt she could not do it herself.\",Vue.h(\"sup\",null,Vue.h(\"a\",{href:\"#footnote-7\",id:\"footnote-ref-7\"},\"7\")),\" Not long afterward, she started HRT.\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.h2,null,\"Help!\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"In that same day’s diary, she had also asked:\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.blockquote,null,\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"And how is someone like me even remotely cute??\",Vue.h(\"sup\",null,Vue.h(\"a\",{href:\"#footnote-8\",id:\"footnote-ref-8\"},\"8\"))),\"\\n\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"Epheia, a cute and kind MtF girl.\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"She would do all she could to help her sisters—whether they were going through a mental health crisis late at night, experiencing violence at home after being involuntarily outed,\",Vue.h(\"sup\",null,Vue.h(\"a\",{href:\"#footnote-9\",id:\"footnote-ref-9\"},\"9\")),\" or being harassed online by cishet people. She helped people find support resources. When she encountered a sister who was suicidal, she would try to buy as much time as she could; once the situation went beyond what she could handle, she would call the police directly.\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"On July 19, I went with her to a meetup with online friends in Nanjing. It was a little after six in the evening, and we were eating when she raised her phone and typed two Chinese characters: “求助!” (“Help!”). One of her sisters had said on Twitter that she was doing very badly, and Epheia was trying to find people who could help her.\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"On July 23, she and a friend carried out a suicide intervention for another sister and also spoke with her parents. She tweeted that she did not know whether they could change her parents’ minds, “but honestly, the atmosphere in her family is so oppressive.” She added that the sister was probably doing okay now, “vibe coding (?”.\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"A healer cannot heal herself.\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"On July 27, 2026, she left us, at just 17 years old.\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"On my GitHub, the collaboration invitation she sent me is still there. It has expired.\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"Epheia, sqrt(-1) STILL ♥️ U\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"Time has walked on into the distance, and so has Epheia. Remember to look back: there was an Epheia who once vibe coded, once watched yuri, once existed here.\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"Dedicated to Epheia (May 12, 2009 ~ July 27, 2026)\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"Sy Yann, written late at night on October 3, 2026, the 68th day since she left us.\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.h2,null,\"What She Left Behind\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"Her website, \",Vue.h(_components.a,{href:\"https://me.epheia.moe/\"},\"me.epheia.moe\"),\", and her tweet archive, \",Vue.h(_components.a,{href:\"https://nyaepheia.pages.dev/\"},\"nyaepheia.pages.dev\"),\", are both still there. They hold the articles and diaries she wrote, along with the things she loved.\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,\"Contributor for this entry: Sy Yann\"),\"\\n\",Vue.h(_components.p,null,Vue.h(_components.strong,null,\"References and Annotations\")),\"\\n\",Vue.h(\"ol\",null,Vue.h(\"li\",{id:\"footnote-1\"},Vue.h(_components.a,{href:\"https://web.archive.org/web/20261003125509/https://epheia.pages.dev/\"},\"Epheia’s Website Homepage (Archived Mirror)\"),Vue.h(\"a\",{href:\"#footnote-ref-1\"},Vue.h(\"svg\",{viewBox:\"0 0 16 16\",version:\"1.1\",id:\"svg1\",